config KLAUSSCPU_VNC_SERVER
	bool "KlaussCPU VNC (RFB) server"
	default n
	depends on NET_SOCKETS
	help
	  Minimal RFB (VNC) server on port 5900 exposing an in-RAM RGB565
	  framebuffer to standard VNC clients (macOS Screen Sharing, TigerVNC,
	  RealVNC).  No VGA hardware required — the framebuffer is served over
	  the network instead of scanned out to a monitor.  Implements the
	  RFB 3.8 mandatory subset (security None, Raw encoding) with per-pixel
	  format conversion.  No auth or TLS — intended for trusted LAN use.
